e action would help a bit more with the race like conditions. ","There were a couple of reasons I did it here instead:\r\n(1) I was trying to modify as little code as possible to avoid introducing some new bug or making things worse\r\n(2) The real problem (in my opinion) isn\u0027t if a single event happens to slip through after the `.watches` shard has been moved -- it\u0027s that we just keep running events until the end of time. This bails out pretty quickly once the `.watches` shard has been moved."],"path":"x-pack/plugin/watcher/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/watcher/trigger/schedule/engine/TickerScheduleTriggerEngine.java","id":37215,"created_at":"2024-07-08T16:36:35Z","original_position":69,"side":"RIGHT","position":69,"submitted_on_commit":"32d6e711546ca5e51db9c03708c294d74fd2e112","diff_hunk":"@@ -106,13 +115,25 @@ public void add(Watch watch) {\n \n     @Override\n     public boolean remove(String jobId) {\n+        logger.debug(\"Removing watch [{}] from engine (engine is running: {})\", jobId, isRunning.get());\n         return schedules.remove(jobId) !\u003d null;\n     }\n \n     void checkJobs() {\n+        if (isRunning.get() \u003d\u003d false) {\n+            logger.debug(\n+                \"Watcher not running because the engine is paused. Currently scheduled watches being skipped: {}\",\n+                schedules.size()\n+            );\n+            return;\n+        }\n         long triggeredTime \u003d clock.millis();\n         List\u003cTriggerEvent\u003e events \u003d new ArrayList\u003c\u003e();\n         for (ActiveSchedule schedule : schedules.values()) {\n+            if (isRunning.get() \u003d\u003d false) {","submitted_line":133},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The check `if (isRunning.get() \u003d\u003d false)` is repeated inside the loop in `checkJobs`. This can lead to unnecessary checks and potential performance issues, especially if the list of schedules is large. Consider moving this check outside the loop or opti